    dict(key='01-poster', kind='poster', title='Dynamic Array (Generic)',
         body=None,
         narration="Hello, and welcome. [[slnc 400]] This video explains the generic dynamic array, in Java. [[slnc 300]] This video is presented by Jayasekhar Konduru. [[slnc 600]] First, a simple definition. [[slnc 300]] A generic dynamic array is an array that grows by itself, written once for any type of element. [[slnc 400]] It stores references to objects, and doubles its room when it is full. [[slnc 700]] Our example is a music playlist of songs. [[slnc 400]] By the end, you will know how Java's array list is built, what a resize really copies, and why deleted places must be cleared."),
